course: dictionary
lesson: 12341
title: Crabby and other moods
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone feels inside, and crabby is one of them. It means grumpy, easily annoyed, or in a bad mood. Look at the clues around it: «Mum was crabby after the long, hungry wait for the bus.» Tired and hungry people often feel crabby, so the clues fit the meaning.
explain: Use the swap check to test your meaning. Put it in the sentence: «Mum was grumpy after the long, hungry wait for the bus.» It still makes sense, so grumpy is a good meaning for crabby.
explain: Crabby is an informal word, so you hear it in everyday talk and in stories more than in formal writing. «The crabby old man shouted at the dog next door.» The shouting is a clue that he is cross and unhappy.
explain: People in different places use different words for the same mood. Crabby is used a lot in the USA and Canada. In the UK, people also say grumpy, ratty or cranky, so «Dad feels ratty today» means much the same as «Dad feels crabby today».
fact: Crabby means grumpy and easily annoyed, in a bad mood.
fact: Crabby is an informal word, so it is used in everyday talk and stories.
fact: A crabby person often snaps at others when they are tired, hungry or unwell.
fact: Crabby is used a lot in the USA and Canada; in the UK people also say grumpy, ratty or cranky.
fact: Phrases to know: «feeling crabby» and «a crabby old man».
exercise: «After the long, hot journey, Sam was very crabby.» What does crabby mean here? | Wet from the rain | Very clean | *Grumpy and in a bad mood | Happy and singing
exercise: «The crabby old man shouted at the children.» Which word shows that the old man was cross? | Children | Old | Man | *Shouted
exercise: Which of these means nearly the same as crabby? | Happy | Brave | Sleepy | *Cranky
test: «Lily felt crabby because she had missed her lunch.» Why might Lily feel crabby? | *She was hungry | She had a new bike | She had won a prize | She was dancing in the park
test: Which sentence shows someone in a crabby mood? | *I am crabby because I did not get any sleep | We are going to the beach today | The baby laughed at the bubbles | The puppy wagged its tail
exam: Which word is used a lot in the USA and Canada for being grumpy? | Glum | Luminous | *Crabby | Barely
